-- title:
--   Cusp at infinity as an A-section of the two-chart model
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $K$ be an intermediate field of the extension $L \subseteq L((q))$ of Laurent series, and let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ the fraction field of $A$, together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be an element, assumed nonzero, whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the rational series $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNumQ`, i.e. of the $q$-expansion `jq` of the modular invariant. Write $A_\infty$ for the subalgebra `chartAlgInf` of $K$ of elements integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$, and let `TwoChartModel` be the pushout of the two morphisms of affine schemes induced by the inclusions of the $j$-chart and the $j^{-1}$-chart algebras into the intermediate algebra, with `modelTo` the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ obtained from the two structure maps. Then there exist a ring homomorphism $\psi : A_\infty \to A$ and a morphism $\varepsilon : \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `TwoChartModel` such that: $\psi$ restricted along $A \to A_\infty$ is the identity; $\psi(j^{-1}) = 0$ (the element `jInvChartInf`); for every $f \in A_\infty$ the image of $\psi(f)$ in $L$ is the coefficient of $q^0$ of $f$ viewed in $L((q))$; $\varepsilon$ is $\operatorname{Spec}\psi$ followed by the chart morphism `ιInf`; $\varepsilon$ followed by `modelTo` is the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} A$; and no point in the image of the underlying map of $\varepsilon$ lies in the range of the underlying map of the other chart morphism `ιFin`.
--
--   This packages the cusp at infinity as an $A$-valued point of the two-chart integral model of the modular curve attached to $K$: the constant-term homomorphism on the $j^{-1}$-chart yields a section of the structure morphism whose image avoids the $j$-finite chart. It is used downstream in the construction of semistable specialisation data with a pinned cusp.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_ringHom_section_comp_iotaInf_modelTo_of_coe_eq_coeffEmb_jq.lean

